Hello All,

The Monthly Sales Team Conference call has March & April scheduled for Mike=
 Friedman with selling UTC into the Utility Market and Phil Busman selling =
3G into the Irrigation Market respectively.  These topics and timing were c=
hosen to support our Philmac initiative going into 2012.   Review of this b=
riefing should be instructive.

In late October we had a meeting with Philmac to review the business.  Atta=
ched is the agenda, sales summary, and Harco 2012 plan brief.  Also attache=
d is the original business plan having more detailed information to provide=
 context.  An example of Distributor UTC buy-in is also attached.

Key Points:


1.       2011 sales (about $450K) are approximately double 2010

2.       Most of the increase is due to 3G increase and in particular due t=
o irrigation market adoption and the acme product

3.       UTC sales are up about 5%.

4.       Goal for 2012 is $1m which is consistent with Philmac=92s goal.

5.       Recently an advertising campaign of small advertisements in four i=
ndustry magazines started in November featuring the UTC.  The idea being th=
at this kind of product will benefit from continuous =93mass=94 exposure.  =
It is essentially our direct mail piece focusing on UTC.

6.       Harco=92s strategic theme remains:  Lead with UTC, cultivate 3G.  =
=93A box of UTC in every truck=94

7.       Mike H. is working with Philmac to develop =93Large Build=94 promo=
tion campaign focusing on creating a bigger advertising program to build aw=
areness.

8.       Philmac has redesigned their ball valve products.  We have recentl=
y received samples to consider.  More on this later.
Current Sales Team Philmac Initiatives Remain:


1.       Develop Larger Municipal adoption and approvals of UTC.

2.       Develop Distributor Branch =93buy in=94 for UTC as good for their =
business.  Attached email on Buckeye State Supply illustrates the =93wild a=
ss cheerleader=94 effect.

3.       Probe for logical 3G opportunities while going about UTC promotion=
 keying off existing use of PE tubing in various applications.  Recent =93n=
o lead=94 movement should improve traction.

4.       Develop irrigation business where PE already in use by exposing pr=
oduct to distributors, contractors, consultants, owners.

Update on compression fitting competitors:


1.       Central Plastics has withdrawn the Alprene product from the market=
.  There may be some residual presence but only until existing inventory is=
 exhausted.

2.       Cepex continues its efforts mostly through =93The Lateral Connecti=
on=94 in the municipal market and through its own efforts in the irrigation=
 market.

3.       Floplast is becoming more aggressive in all markets with tradeshow=
 activities.

4.       Nupi has limited effort targeted at the geothermal application.

John

